This program uses the `libgpiod` and `pigpio` libraries to communicate with the MAX30102 sensor over I2C and GPIO, respectively. It initializes the I2C and GPIO handles, reads the Part ID register to verify sensor presence, and then continuously reads the SpO2 and heart rate registers once per second. If either value falls below the threshold, it writes a log entry to a file named `health_log.txt` prefixed with an ISO 8601 timestamp. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by properly releasing the I2C and GPIO handles and exiting gracefully.

