This code uses the `pigpio` library to interface with the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and SPI peripherals. It initializes the `pigpio` library, opens a handle to the SPI bus and a handle to the GPIO pin connected to the buzzer, and sets up a signal handler to handle the `SIGINT` signal (Ctrl-C).

The main loop reads the analog output of the MQ-2 gas sensor through the MCP3008 ADC connected on SPI0 using CE0 (GPIO8, BCM) and channel 0, and drives the buzzer attached to GPIO24 (BCM) based on the ADC reading. The buzzer is turned off when the ADC reading is below the threshold value of 500 and turned on when the reading is equal to or exceeds 500.

The code checks for errors in every init and syscall, and handles errors by printing an error message and continuing to the next iteration of the main loop. It also handles the `SIGINT` signal by closing the SPI handle, resetting the GPIO states to a safe condition, and invoking the library's cleanup API call.

