This code uses the `libgpiod` and `pigpio` libraries to interact with the GPIO and SPI interfaces on the Raspberry Pi. It reads the moisture level from the Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to channel 0 of an MCP3008 ADC on SPI0 (CE0 on GPIO 8, 1 MHz, mode 0), compares the reading to a configurable threshold (default 30% of the 0-3V range), and activates a relay-driven water pump on GPIO 18 (BCM, active-high) for a configurable duration (default 10 seconds) when the moisture level falls below that threshold. The program accepts command-line options `-t` for threshold, `-d` for pump duration in seconds, and `-s` for the sleep interval, and logs every moisture reading and each pump activation or deactivation with timestamps to a file named `irrigation.log`. It handles SPI communication errors by retrying up to three times per read and, if all retries fail, logs the error and skips that irrigation cycle without turning on the pump. On receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM, the program ensures the pump is turned off, closes the SPI interface, terminates any driver usage, and exits cleanly, guaranteeing the pump is off on all exit paths including any failure to open the SPI bus.

