This code uses the `libgpiod` library to access the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up a signal handler for SIGINT to handle the Ctrl-C interrupt and gracefully shut down the program. The main loop reads the GPIO pins, converts the values to magnetic field strength, and writes the values to a log file. The program checks for out-of-range values and skips the logging for that iteration if any GPIO read fails. The program also handles errors and releases all driver resources properly on all exit paths.

