This program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi, and the `libspi` library to interact with the SPI bus. It also uses the `libi2c` library to interact with the I2C bus.

The program first initializes the BH1750 light sensor, MAX4466 microphone, and MCP3008 ADC using the `bh1750_init()`, `max4466_init()`, and `mcp3008_init()` functions, respectively.

The program then enters an infinite loop that reads the light and sound levels from the sensors using the `bh1750_read()`, `max4466_read()`, and `mcp3008_read()` functions, respectively. It then formats the data into a string using the `strftime()` function and appends it to a file named `environmental_log.txt` using the `fprintf()` function.

The program handles any errors that may occur during the initialization, reading, or writing of the sensors by printing an error message to the console and returning an error code. It also ensures that all resources are cleanly released and the program terminates gracefully on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM by using the `close()` function to close the file descriptors for the I2C and SPI buses.

