```
This code uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up the row anodes and column cathodes as outputs, and then scans the columns left to right, clearing the matrix before each column by setting all column cathodes HIGH and all row anodes LOW, and then for each column sets the column cathode LOW and lights the LEDs sequentially by setting the corresponding row anodes HIGH. It also sets up a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM to clean up on exit.

Note that this code assumes that the row anodes and column cathodes are connected to the GPIO pins as specified in the problem statement. If the connections are different, the code will need to be modified accordingly.

