This code uses the `libgpiod` library to communicate with the I2C bus and the `localtime` function from the `time.h` header to get the current time. It also uses the `strftime` function from the `time.h` header to format the time string.

The code first opens the I2C bus and sets the slave address to the address of the Sensirion SDP800-500Pa sensor. It then opens the log file for writing and enters an infinite loop.

In each iteration of the loop, the code sends the continuous measurement command to the sensor, waits for the conversion time, reads the pressure data, validates the CRC, extracts the pressure data, gets the current time, and logs the pressure reading to the log file.

The code then sleeps for `LOG_INTERVAL` seconds before repeating the process.

When the program receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal, it cleans up by closing the I2C handle, flushing and closing the log file, and terminating the driver library gracefully.

