The `init_handlers` function sets up the signal handlers for `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM`, which will set the `running` flag to `false` when the signals are received. The `close_handlers` function restores the default signal handlers.

The `write_csv_header` function writes the header row to the CSV file, and the `write_csv_row` function writes a new row to the file with the current timestamp and pressure reading.

The `read_pressure` function opens the I2C bus, reads the pressure reading from the sensor, and writes the data to the CSV file. If the pressure reading is outside the safe range, it prints a warning to `stderr`. If there is an error reading the pressure, it closes the I2C handle and returns.

The `main` function sets up the signal handlers, opens the CSV file, and enters a loop that reads the pressure every second and writes it to the file. When the `running` flag is set to `false` by the signal handlers, the loop exits and the program terminates.

