This code uses the `libgpiod` library to communicate with the Sensirion SDP810-500Pa sensor over I2C. It sends the measurement command, waits 45 ms, reads the data, reads the CRC, validates the CRC, extracts the temperature and pressure, checks for sensor absence, pressure out of range, and temperature out of range, and prints the results to the log file and stdout. It also checks for a warning if the pressure exceeds 5 Pa. The code handles I2C read/write failures, CRC mismatches, and the case where the sensor is absent, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM it cleans up the I2C handle, closes the log file, and invokes the library's `libgpiod_cleanup()` function.

