This program uses the `libgpiod` library to communicate with the SCD40 sensor over I2C, and the `pthread` library to create a separate logging thread. The program uses a circular buffer to store the CO₂, temperature, and humidity readings, and a mutex to ensure thread safety. The main loop waits at least one second after issuing the start-periodic-measurement command before the first read, then reads the sensor every five seconds, validating the CRC-8 of each value using the polynomial and initial value documented for the device. On any CRC failure or I2C read/write error, the program logs the error and skips that reading. The logging thread writes the buffered records to the CSV file every sixty seconds. The program handles SIGINT by using a volatile `sig_atomic_t` running flag to stop the main loop, send the documented stop-periodic-measurement command, join the logging thread, flush any remaining buffered data to a final CSV file, close the I2C handle, and cleanly terminate the driver without any resource leaks.

