This code sets up the Raspberry Pi to interface with the BMP180 sensor on the I2C bus, reads the sensor's calibration data and applies the Bosch compensation formulas to compute pressure in pascals, and toggles data logging on and off via a falling-edge interrupt on GPIO27 with a 200 ms debounce. While logging is enabled, the program records a timestamp and the computed pressure to a file named `pressure_log.txt` every 2 seconds. The program also detects and recovers from I2C communication errors and driver initialization failures, and cleans up all allocated resources and gracefully terminates when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

