This code sets up the Raspberry Pi to interface with the TI AWR1642 mmWave radar sensor over SPI channel 0 (CE0/GPIO8) at 1 MHz, mode 0, using a hardware frame trigger on GPIO23 (BCM) and a data-ready interrupt on GPIO24 (BCM) to capture range-Doppler heatmap frames at a 100 ms period. The sensor is pre-configured via the TI mmWave SDK to stream range-Doppler data, with a configuration struct that records a start frequency of 77 GHz, end frequency of 79 GHz, 64 chirps, and 256 samples, and each frame requires a full-duplex SPI transfer of 32,768 bytes of heatmap data. The code logs the data to a binary file whose header contains the documented magic number 4144, an 8-byte timestamp, and the configuration struct, followed by per-frame timestamps and frame numbers. The code checks all return codes, handles any memory allocation failures, and ensures that on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM the program gracefully closes the SPI device, releases the GPIO pins, and closes the log file.

