In the main loop, it reads the sensor value and turns the LED on if the sensor is active, and off otherwise. It then sleeps for the poll interval before repeating the process.

When the program receives a `SIGINT` or `SIGTERM` signal, it turns the LED off, releases the resources, and exits.

Note that this code assumes that the LED is connected to GPIO18 (physical pin 12, BCM 18) and the sensor is connected to GPIO23 (physical pin 16, BCM 23). If your connections are different, you will need to modify the code accordingly.

