This code uses the `pigpio` library to interface with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up the LED and buzzer pins as outputs, and the flame sensor pin as an input. It then performs a self-test by blinking the LED twice and reading the flame sensor five times at 100ms intervals, and if any read returns LOW, it signals an error by blinking the LED rapidly and sounding the buzzer with a short-short-long-short pattern.

If the self-test is successful, the program enters a main loop that polls the flame sensor every 50ms, and if a LOW is observed, the buzzer and LED are turned on continuously until a subsequent read returns HIGH, at which point they are turned off. All events (flame detected, flame cleared, any errors) are logged with timestamps to a file called `flame_sensor.log`.

The program also sets up a signal handler to catch SIGINT and clean up the GPIO lines before exiting.

