This code uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the I2C bus and the `pigpio` library to handle the GPIO pins. It first opens the I2C bus and verifies the WHO_AM_I identifier of the FXOS8700CQ sensor. It then puts the device in standby mode, configures it for a ±2 g range and a 200 Hz output data rate, and activates it.

The main loop reads the acceleration data from the sensor, computes the acceleration magnitude, and checks if it exceeds the impact threshold. If it does, it gets the current timestamp, writes a line to the impact log file, and continues the loop.

The code handles errors by printing a diagnostic message to stderr and continuing the loop rather than crashing. It also handles the SIGINT signal by gracefully closing the I2C handle, invoking the appropriate library shutdown call, and exiting cleanly.

