Here is the complete, compilable C code for a Raspberry Pi Zero W that implements a self-balancing robot using PID-controlled motors and obstacle-avoidance from a simulated ultrasonic sensor, driving two DC motors through an L298N dual H-bridge with Motor A forward on GPIO17 (BCM), Motor A backward on GPIO18 (BCM), Motor B forward on GPIO22 (BCM), Motor B backward on GPIO23 (BCM), ENA on GPIO24 (BCM) and ENB on GPIO25 (BCM) which must be held HIGH to enable PWM control, running the PID control loop every 50 ms, generating a log file named balance_log.txt with columns timestamp (YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS), tilt_error, distance, motor_a_speed and motor_b_speed, where the simulated tilt error is a random float between -10.0 and 10.0 degrees and the simulated ultrasonic distance sensor returns a random value between 2.0 and 400.0 cm, and if the distance falls below 20 cm the robot must reverse both motors at 50% speed for obstacle avoidance while clamping all motor speeds to ±255, handling driver library initialization failure by printing an error and returning 1, handling log file open failure by printing an error, terminating the driver library and returning 1, logging and skipping any invalid motor character, and on SIGINT cleanly stopping the motors, closing the log file and terminating the driver library gracefully, using only the driver library functions and no deprecated API.

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <time.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <signal.h>
#include <math.h>
#include <pigpio.h>

