The code also handles I2C open or configuration errors by performing cleanup (closing the bus and terminating the driver library) and exiting with code 0 in non‑hardware environments. It also handles sensor read errors by returning zeros and continuing.

Finally, the code installs a SIGINT handler that gracefully terminates by closing I2C and shutting down the driver library.

