```
This program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It initializes the GPIO chip and requests lines for the two valves, and then sets up signal handlers for `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` to handle termination of the program.

The main loop of the program repeatedly activates and deactivates the valves, logging each activation event to a file named `valve_log.txt`. The program exits cleanly on receipt of a `SIGINT` or `SIGTERM` signal, releasing the GPIO lines and closing the log file.

Note that this program assumes that the valves are controlled only via their relays (i.e., GPIO HIGH = relay ON = valve OPEN, GPIO LOW = relay OFF = valve CLOSED). If the valves are controlled by other means, such as a separate control circuit, this program may not work correctly.

